Original commit body from 040c31f1f2ef8dbb7b25b7c15627d1bc5598ccf5:

A call outside every function is anchored on the node it runs in: the
file for module-level code (`_REGISTRY = _build_registry()`), the class
for a class body or a static initializer. Nothing said when an anchor is
itself reached, and four consumers disagreed on one fixture:

* dead-code-maybe walked from function/method seeds over call edges and
  never entered an anchor, so a module-init helper read dead under
  `--seeds entrypoints`, and under the default seeds when private
  (lib.py `_build_registry` imported by main.py);
* test-coverage and sketch's coverage line likewise, so production helpers
  reached from a test module's module-level code or a test class body were
  cold spots;
* the test-only ratchet counted any caller in a test file, anchors
  included -- the right answer, since the runner imports test modules.

New module anchor_execution writes the contract down and serves it as
walk-only edges from the graph's own `contains` and file-to-file `imports`
edges: member -> container (calling a function requires its module, using
a member its class), file -> the type-like symbols it contains (loading a
module runs its class bodies), importer file -> imported file. The three
walking consumers add them to the graph they walk, the way INV-rolok's
construction-initializer edges are added; nothing is emitted. Containing
is still not calling: no edge leads from a container to a function, so a
loaded file makes its module-level code and class bodies run, never a
function nobody calls -- each test fixture keeps such a function and it
stays dead / cold.

No separate test seed: a test function reaches its own test class and
test module through the member -> container step, so the walks agree with
the ratchet without counting a test FILE as a test (a first cut seeded
test-file anchors and raised fastapi's reported total_tests 3768 -> 4535;
dropped). Residual, documented: a test file with module-level calls and
no test function or class is not reached.

Measured against dev on the same survey map (dev tree on PYTHONPATH):
  django   dead (entrypoints) 8,581 -> 8,297; dead (production) 1,364 ->
           1,353; test-coverage tested 1,917 -> 1,960 (19.0% -> 19.5%);
           test-coverage 3.5s -> 4.6s; none newly dead (edges are only
           added). Samples read against source: OLMapWidget.js's MapWidget
           methods (constructed inside a module-level
           document.addEventListener registration), multipartparser's
           InterBoundaryIter.__init__.
  fastapi  dead (entrypoints) 1,233 -> 1,165; production 120 unchanged;
           tested 38 -> 41; total_tests unchanged.

Tests: core unit (each edge rule; a loaded file never reaches its
functions; live-object shape) and production path (run_behavior_map +
dead-code-maybe under entrypoints/production/tests seeds, test-coverage
cold spots, sketch's _estimate_test_coverage).

